IMPORT prelude

-- States of Malaya Customs Duties Collection Act 1958 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a traveller, importer, exporter, agent
-- or owner of goods at a Malaysian customs collection station in Singapore: authority cards (s 7(2)), refunds and short-paid duty
-- (ss 10, 11), abatement (s 12), declaration before loading and on export (ss 14(1), 15(1)), unpaid export duty and uncleared goods
-- (ss 15(3)-(5), 26), the proceeds of a sale (ss 11(3), (4), 15(3), (5), 26(3), (4)), search of passengers (s 29), seized goods with
-- no prosecution (s 41), compounding (ss 19(2), 43), costs and damages (s 44), the offences and penalties a person meets (ss 16(5),
-- 45, 46, 47, 49), imprisonment in default of a fine (s 36), and directors (s 51(1)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SMCDCA1958.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest
-- amending Act in its legislative history is Act 15 of 2010 (Criminal Procedure Code 2010, in force 2 January 2011), and the latest
-- annotation in the body is [15/2010] at s 30. THE s 36 TABLE IS COLUMN-SHIFTED IN THE .txt DEPOSIT: the periods "2 months",
-- "4 months", "6 months" appear one line above the bands they belong to; they were matched to bands (a), (b), (c) by order.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0256 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the provisions such a person meets. Not encoded: appointments and officers' status (ss 3-6),
-- establishment of stations and valuation (ss 8, 9, 13), postal examination beyond the forfeiture and compounding of s 19, document
-- production, sampling and handling charges (ss 21-23), the protection from loss in custody (s 25), powers to open, seize and stop
-- (ss 27, 28), prosecution and evidence rules (ss 30-35, 37-40, 42) beyond what is named above, bribery (s 48), rewards and
-- regulations (ss 52-56). The Malaysian duty rates themselves (s 13) come from the Malaysian Customs Act 1967 and are not here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `States of Malaya Customs Duties Collection Act 1958 -- collection`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `7(2) -- officers not in uniform`

-- s 7(1): an officer "if not in uniform, on demand declare his office and produce ... such authority card as the Collector may
-- direct". (2): "It shall not be an offence for any person to refuse to comply with any request, demand or order" of such an
-- officer "if that officer is not in uniform and refuses to declare his office and produce his authority card, on demand being made
-- by that person".
GIVEN `officer in uniform` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person demanded the card` IS A BOOLEAN, `officer declared office and produced card` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing the officer is not an offence` IF
    (NOT `officer in uniform`) AND `the person demanded the card` AND (NOT `officer declared office and produced card`)

§§ `10, 11 -- refunds and short-paid duty`

-- s 10: the Collector may order a refund of money "overpaid as customs duty or other charges" if proved to his satisfaction,
-- "Provided that no such refund shall be allowed unless a claim in respect thereof is made within one year after the overpayment".
GIVEN `overpayment proved` IS A BOOLEAN, `months from overpayment to claim` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a refund may be ordered` IF
    `overpayment proved` AND `months from overpayment to claim` AT MOST 12

-- s 11(1): duty short paid "through inadvertence, error, collusion or misconstruction" of an officer, a misstatement "or for any other
-- reason", or erroneously refunded, must be paid "on demand being made within 12 months from the date on which customs duty was
-- payable or deficient customs duty was paid or the refund was made". The person's dutiable goods in a station may be detained.
GIVEN `months to the demand` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the short-paid duty must be paid on the demand` IF
    `months to the demand` AT MOST 12

§§ `12 -- abatement after payment`

-- s 12: "After payment of customs duty, no abatement of such duty shall be allowed on any goods on account of damage", or a claim to a
-- preferential rate, or that the weight, measure, volume or value determined by the officer is incorrect, "unless notice in writing
-- of the claim has been given at or before the time of the payment".
GIVEN `written notice given at or before payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an abatement may be allowed` IF
    `written notice given at or before payment`

§§ `14(1), 15(1) -- declaring and paying`

-- s 14(1): goods to be imported into Malaysia "shall not be loaded for despatch" until the importer or consignor has (a) made a
-- declaration in the prescribed form and (b) paid the import duty and other charges -- "Provided that such declaration and payment
-- ... shall not be required" if the owner consents to consign the goods to a customs warehouse or licensed warehouse in Malaysia.
GIVEN `declaration made` IS A BOOLEAN, `duty and charges paid` IS A BOOLEAN, `consigned to a Malaysian warehouse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods may be loaded for despatch` IF
    (`declaration made` AND `duty and charges paid`) OR `consigned to a Malaysian warehouse`

-- s 15(1): an exporter or consignee must declare and pay export duty, "Provided that such declaration shall not be required" where
-- it is shown to the officer's satisfaction "that export duty has been paid at a customs station in Malaysia".
GIVEN `export duty shown paid in Malaysia` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an export declaration is required` IF
    NOT `export duty shown paid in Malaysia`

§§ `15(3)-(5), 26 -- unpaid duty and uncleared goods`

-- s 15(3): if export duty "is not paid within 3 months from the time when possession of them was taken" by an officer, "the goods
-- shall be sold by public auction"; (4) particulars published in the Gazette "not less than 14 days prior to the date of the sale".
GIVEN `months since possession taken` IS A NUMBER, `export duty paid` IS A BOOLEAN, `days of Gazette notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the export goods must be auctioned now` IF
    (NOT `export duty paid`) AND `months since possession taken` GREATER THAN 3 AND `days of Gazette notice` AT LEAST 14

-- s 26(1): goods deposited "for a period exceeding 4 days reckoned from the date of deposit" may be removed by the Collector, who
-- has a lien for expenses. (2): goods "not cleared ... within a period of one month reckoned from the date of deposit" may be sold
-- after "not less than 14 days' notice in writing to the owner (if the name and address of the owner are known to him)" or 14 days'
-- notice in the Gazette (if not). s 11(2) uses the same notice rule for goods detained for short-paid duty.
GIVEN `days since deposit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Collector may remove the goods` IF
    `days since deposit` GREATER THAN 4

GIVEN `whole months since deposit` IS A NUMBER, `cleared` IS A BOOLEAN, `owner's address known` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days of written notice to owner` IS A NUMBER, `days of Gazette notice given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Collector may sell uncleared goods` IF
    (NOT `cleared`) AND `whole months since deposit` AT LEAST 1
    AND (    (`owner's address known` AND `days of written notice to owner` AT LEAST 14)
          OR ((NOT `owner's address known`) AND `days of Gazette notice given` AT LEAST 14))

§§ `11(3), (4), 15(3), (5), 26(3), (4) -- what a sale yields`

-- The proceeds pay first "the charges that have been occasioned by the sale" and then the duty and other charges, "and the surplus,
-- if any, shall be paid to the owner ... and if the owner cannot be found within one month of the sale, the surplus shall be paid to
-- the general revenue of Malaysia". If "no sufficient bid is forthcoming to satisfy the customs duty and charges", the goods "shall
-- be forfeited to the government of Malaysia". (Inference: the sale charges are counted with the duty and charges in deciding
-- whether a bid is sufficient; the text says only "customs duty and charges".)
GIVEN `proceeds` IS A NUMBER, `sale charges` IS A NUMBER, `duty and other charges` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the surplus` MEANS
    `the greater of` (`proceeds` MINUS `sale charges` MINUS `duty and other charges`) 0

GIVEN `best bid` IS A NUMBER, `sale charges` IS A NUMBER, `duty and other charges` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods are forfeited for want of a sufficient bid` IF
    `best bid` LESS THAN `sale charges` PLUS `duty and other charges`

GIVEN `owner found within one month of the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surplus goes to the owner` IF
    `owner found within one month of the sale`

§§ `29 -- search of passengers`

-- s 29: a person leaving for Malaysia by aircraft or railway must on demand permit his person, goods and baggage to be searched,
-- "Provided that -- (a) any person who requests that his person be searched in the presence of a Federal Superintendent ... shall
-- not be searched except in the presence of and under the supervision of that officer; (b) the goods and baggage of any person who
-- requests to be present ... and so presents himself within a reasonable time shall not be searched except in his presence; (c) no
-- woman shall be searched except by a woman."
GIVEN `passenger is a woman` IS A BOOLEAN, `searcher is a woman` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `asked for a Superintendent` IS A BOOLEAN, `Superintendent present and supervising` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the search of the person may proceed` IF
        (NOT (`passenger is a woman` AND (NOT `searcher is a woman`)))
    AND (NOT (`asked for a Superintendent` AND (NOT `Superintendent present and supervising`)))

GIVEN `asked to be present` IS A BOOLEAN, `came within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN, `passenger present` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the baggage search may proceed` IF
    (NOT (`asked to be present` AND `came within a reasonable time`)) OR `passenger present`

§§ `41, 44 -- seized goods`

-- s 41(1): with no prosecution, seized goods "shall be taken and deemed to be forfeited at the expiration of one calendar month from
-- the date of seizure unless a claim thereto is made before that date"; (2) the claim is written notice to the Collector.
GIVEN `prosecution brought` IS A BOOLEAN, `whole calendar months since seizure` IS A NUMBER, `written claim made in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seized goods are deemed forfeited` IF
    (NOT `prosecution brought`) AND `whole calendar months since seizure` AT LEAST 1 AND (NOT `written claim made in time`)

-- s 44: no person is "entitled to the costs of the proceedings or to any damages or other relief other than an order for the return
-- of the goods or the payment of their value unless the seizure was made without reasonable or probable cause".
GIVEN `seizure without reasonable or probable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `costs or damages may be awarded for the seizure` IF
    `seizure without reasonable or probable cause`

§§ `19(2), 43 -- compounding`

-- s 19(2): a Federal Superintendent may compound by accepting from the addressee or consignor of a postal article "a sum not
-- exceeding $500" and release it on payment of the duty. s 43(1): a Superintendent, any prescribed compoundable offence, "a sum not
-- exceeding $500"; (2) a Federal Customs Officer, an offence "prescribed to be compoundable by that officer", "not exceeding $20".
-- (3) on payment the suspect is discharged, seized property released, "no further proceedings".
DECLARE Compounder IS ONE OF
    `a Federal Superintendent`
    `a Federal Customs Officer`
    `a Superintendent for a postal article`

GIVEN `who compounds` IS A Compounder
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be accepted to compound` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who compounds`
    WHEN `a Federal Customs Officer` THEN 20
    OTHERWISE 500

§§ `16(5), 45, 46, 47, 49 -- offences and penalties`

-- s 16(5): acting as agent without permission, or declaring goods without authority -- "a fine not exceeding $500".
-- s 45: a declaration or document "untrue or incorrect in any material particular" -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000".
-- s 47: assaulting or obstructing an officer, rescuing seized goods, destroying packages -- (d) first offence "a fine not exceeding
-- $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 9 months or to both"; (e) second or subsequent "a fine not exceeding $5,000 AND
-- to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 18 months".
-- s 49: any other contravention "for which no penalty is expressly provided" -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `acting as an agent without permission`
    `an incorrect declaration`
    `obstructing an officer, first offence`
    `obstructing an officer, repeat offence`
    `a contravention with no penalty provided`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `acting as an agent without permission` THEN 500
    WHEN `an incorrect declaration` THEN 5000
    WHEN `obstructing an officer, first offence` THEN 2000
    WHEN `obstructing an officer, repeat offence` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `obstructing an officer, first offence` THEN 9
    WHEN `obstructing an officer, repeat offence` THEN 18
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `imprisonment is mandatory` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `obstructing an officer, repeat offence` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 46: unlawfully removing goods from a station, or tampering with declared goods or baggage before import --
-- (c)(i) dutiable goods, first offence: "not less than 6 times the amount of the customs duty or $5,000, whichever is the lesser
-- amount, and of not more than 20 times the amount of the customs duty or $5,000 whichever is the greater amount" (where the duty
-- cannot be ascertained, not exceeding $5,000); (c)(ii) second or subsequent: "such fine or to imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 2 years or to both";
-- (d) non-dutiable or prohibited goods: "not less than twice the value of the goods or $5,000, whichever is the lesser amount, and
-- of not more than 5 times the value of the goods or $5,000 whichever is the greater amount".
GIVEN `the duty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum s 46 fine for dutiable goods` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (6 TIMES `the duty`) 5000

GIVEN `the duty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum s 46 fine for dutiable goods` MEANS
    `the greater of` (20 TIMES `the duty`) 5000

GIVEN `the value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum s 46 fine for other goods` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (2 TIMES `the value`) 5000

GIVEN `the value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum s 46 fine for other goods` MEANS
    `the greater of` (5 TIMES `the value`) 5000

§§ `36 -- imprisonment in default of a fine`

-- s 36: the default term "shall not exceed in any case the maximum fixed by the following scale": (a) fine not exceeding $25 --
-- 2 months; (b) exceeding $25 but not $50 -- 4 months; (c) exceeding $50 but not $100 -- 6 months; "with 2 additional months for
-- every $100 after the first $100 of the fine until a maximum period of 3 years is reached". (Periods matched to bands by order;
-- see the header. Inference: only each complete $100 after the first $100 adds 2 months.)
GIVEN `remaining` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the additional months for each further $100` MEANS
    IF `remaining` AT LEAST 100 THEN 2 PLUS `the additional months for each further $100` (`remaining` MINUS 100) ELSE 0

GIVEN `the fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the longest default imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `the fine` AT MOST 25 THEN 2
    ELSE IF `the fine` AT MOST 50 THEN 4
        ELSE IF `the fine` AT MOST 100 THEN 6
            ELSE `the lesser of` (6 PLUS `the additional months for each further $100` (`the fine` MINUS 100)) 36

§§ `51(1) -- directors and officers`

-- s 51(1): where a company, firm or society commits an offence, a director, manager, secretary, similar officer or partner "shall be
-- deemed to be guilty of that offence unless he proves that the offence was committed without his consent or connivance and that he
-- exercised all such diligence to prevent the commission of the offence as he ought to have exercised".
GIVEN `the body committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `was an officer or partner at the time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved no consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is deemed guilty` IF
    `the body committed the offence` AND `was an officer or partner at the time`
    AND (NOT (`proved no consent or connivance` AND `proved due diligence`))
